// Knights and Knaves puzzle (classic logic puzzle)
// Knights always tell the truth, knaves always lie

// Person A says: "B is a knight"
// Person B says: "A is a knave"

// If A is a knight, then B is a knight: A -> B
// If A is a knave, then B is not a knight: -A -> -B
// If B is a knight, then A is a knave: B -> -A
// If B is a knave, then A is not a knave: -B -> A

((A -> B) & (-A -> -B)) & ((B -> -A) & (-B -> A))
